A||N||8||rprevo||Late 70's GM High Energy Ignition||||1||
Z||000000||rprevo||02-27-2001||10:45 PM|||| This is a strange problem to me,<BR>Small block chevy crate motor, All new<BR>distrib parts, COIL, PICK-UP COIL, Module<BR>Cap Rotor, GM Performance wires and delco <BR>plugs, 9.5 to 1 compresion 330 hp crate.<BR>Holley 750 double pumper. 70 Jets.<BR> Any way engine runs awsome wash the car<BR>and engine gets a little wet, Bank closest<BR>to the fire wall in the Fiero seems to quit<BR>running properly, Meaning as the engine runs<BR>a miss fire shoots fireballs out of the tail pipe, Pop Pop Pop repeatedly, Removed plug wires tell we discovered the offenders and<BR>replaced them, Engine ran  awsome. Wash the<BR>car engine does the same thing again,<BR>Now to eliminate varibles we put a super coil<BR>another new cap Rotor Accell wires and plugs.<BR>Ran like a raped ape untill car was washed,<BR>Same problem again. Now I have the same set<BR>up in my Fiero same dist components 5000 miles on it and I think my small block could<BR>be submerged in water and the thing would stay running. I am in pretty good understanding of the first GM HEI Dist's<BR>but aint never seen this happen, If there is someone out there that can give me somthing<BR>else to look for in the problem I would give many thanks,<P>    Ray,<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||02-28-2001||06:12 AM||||Might check the plug wires on both ends for arcing. Moisture may be entering the boots and shorting to the adjacent plug creating the miss-fire condition.||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FST2M6||02-28-2001||08:16 AM||||spray the inside of the cap with WD-40 it'll displace any water that get up in there.. (do this on the UniMOG, my friends Jeep and my Former 95 Splash 4x4) never had stalling issues in the mud or pressure washer again. odds are it's not the wires it's the cap.. most don't have splash shields and even fewer have o-ring seal provisions.||||reg||1
Z||000003||rprevo||02-28-2001||10:30 PM|||| I will check the one for moisture and<BR>take the advice of the WD-40 I have a friend<BR>that has a Uni-Mog he got it last year in<BR>Germany, Very cool Ultimate SUV<P>Many thanks, <P>    Ray,||||reg||1
Z||000004||Songman||03-02-2001||02:19 AM||||Or just quit washing the car... heheh<P>Sorry.. that is the type of advice I get around Nashville...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||bubbajoexx||03-02-2001||11:50 PM||||use silicone grease on all the boots and you will have no more moisture problems||||reg||1
Z||000006||rprevo||03-03-2001||04:37 AM|||| Is Silicon grease the same as Dielectric<BR>Grease? We're going to work on it this<BR>weekend.<P> Thanks again for all the insight.<P>Ray<BR> ||||reg||6
Z||000007||Blaster||03-04-2001||01:22 AM||||Ok... first off, did you try the night test? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> You know, firing it up at night and see if you have any arcs. If it doesn't do it dry then try this. Get a spray bottle, put it on mist and spray around a little then fire her up. (GM mechanic did it, I swear. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)<P>Later.||||reg||1
Z||000008||rprevo||03-04-2001||06:22 AM|||| Well in conclusion these are the things<BR>we did yesterday.<BR> 1.. We used the silicon grease in all the<BR>     boots and on the rim seal of the cap.<BR> 2.. We put a new coating of grease under the      Module.<BR> 3.. We put a ground strap on the head            closest to the firewall. <BR>      The Batery is in the trunk and the negetive cable in mounted to the head near the trunk the ground for the whole car is mounted on the lower portion of the block<BR>near the firewall. The exaust attached to that head is hung by rubber insulated hangers  I think that when the car gets wet that the head shorts out like the boots get the least bit damp and plugs don't fire. So anyway with  all the silicon grease sealling the travel of electricity and the head compleatly grounded for sure I'm happy to say that the<BR>engine was soaked with the garden hose and fired up with no problem and we smoked a T/A WS6 with no problem.<BR> I really appoligize for the long reply<BR>but I just wanted to let the people who gave me help in solving this problem know that it's appreciated.<P>  Ray<P>        ||||reg||10
